{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463612-v20-touchstone-background","id":1463612,"title":"[V20] Touchstone Background","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-12T13:29:05-07:00","id":1463612,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [V20] Touchstone Background","content":"Okay so...I was looking at random stuff when I found this post on Reddit: <a href=\"http://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/oxvhhv/comment/h7p2z7v/?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=web2x&amp;context=3\" target=\"_blank\">The Reddit Post</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ASharpYoungMan from Reddit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">While I'm a big V20 proponent (and I think you should go with your gut and use V20 rules with V5 metaplot), a few suggestions on how you might snag a few of V5's improvements:</span></span></span><ul><li>I suggest folding some of the aspects of the <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Composure</span> Attribute into <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Appearance</span> (i.e., have Appearance be about body language, bearing, and general presence, in addition to looks, style, and grooming). This works out splendidly, and makes Appearance feel more active.<ul><li>I suggest keeping the Attribute name &quot;Appearance&quot; - it fits the tone of Vampire so well (though I like Composure too).</li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Resolve</span> is an utterly fucking useless Attribute (there's already a Willpower trait, there's no need for a Willpower Attribute as well). Keep <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Perception</span> - it's 10x as useful.<ul><li>Alternatively, if you like the idea of Resolve, you could fold aspects of Resolve into Perception, and call the Attribute &quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Focus</span>&quot; - it has all the connotations of both of the other attributes, without being the sad, sorry, redundant thing that Resolve became. But ultimately, Perception just works, so no need to mess with it. Self-Control and Courage can do everything Resolve can do, anyway.</li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Loresheets</span> are awesome, and you might consider allowing players to buy them with Background points and Freebie points (1:1 - might require a little conversion in some cases).</li> <li>Consider creating a background called &quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Touchstones</span>&quot; - these would be like V5 Touchstones (but also expanded to include non-persons, like keepsakes or mementos that remind you of your mortal life). Each dot is 1 extra die that can be used (once per Story) on Conscience rolls to resist Humanity loss.</li> <li>I strongly recommend you consider ditching the following lore uptdates:<ul><li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The Beckoning</span>. Half the fun of Vampire is the Elders lurking in their shadowy high-rises. The game loses so much of it's bite if Elders peace out. If you want to reduce the Elder population, have them go into hiding as a result of the SI (like they did when the first inquisition came around - they hid and threw their childer to the witch hunters - a tactic that caused the Vampire Hysteria to die down after a couple of centuries - this should be standard operating procedure for Elder Camarilla).<ul><li>This is also eerie for neonates. You hear stories of powerful elders... but you also hear that they're going to ground. Something is happening... something that isn't good.</li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The Hecata</span>. The mental gymnastics needed to justify the disparate bloodlines of the shattered Cappadocian clan turning around and forming their own &quot;Clan&quot; are manifold, and again, it loses something if these bitter rivalries are subdued. That said, from the outside, it must be <i>fucking terrifying</i> to see Harbingers and Giovanni shacking up together. Something must have spooked them enough (or some<i>thing</i> is making a major move in the Jyhad) to let bygones be bygones...</li> </ul></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>So this inspired me to do a few things. First, I am working on making a character sheet that reflect these suggested rules, because I like them. However, I am also making this post to document my idea for how the Touchstones background could work. So here you go:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Touchstones</b></span><br /> <i>This Background is for Vampires with Humanity only.</i><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A Touchstone is part of the mortal world, usually a living, breathing person. Rarely, it can be a place or thing. These touchstones act as representations of human values and ethics for the vampire to project to relate to. As a result, touchstones can not be vampires or any other supernatural being, as these creatures are distant from one\u2019s original humanity. For every dot in this background, the vampire receives a touchstone, which they should describe.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Touchstones also act as an anchor for the vampire\u2019s humanity, and work to guard against degeneration. Each dot in the Background provides a bonus die to Conscience rolls made to avoid degeneration. This bonus applies as long as the vampire maintains a meaningful relationship with the Touchstones. This bonus is limited by the vampire total humanity, and the Conscience dice pool still can not be more than the vampire\u2019s humanity score.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">However, this Background is a double-edged sword. If a touchstone were to be damaged or destroyed, as such, the touchstone dies or is wounded, the vampire must roll for Degeneration without the Touchstone dice bonus. In addition, any botch on Degeneration reduces the background\u2019s rating by 1, and a touchstone of the Storyteller\u2019s choice is lost. Finally, touchstones are always considered loved ones for the purposes of Frenzy, regardless of the actual relationship or if the touchstone is even a person.<br /> <br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Optional Rule: Associated Ethics</span><br /> This rule is to further define the role of touchstones by having each touchstone had an associated ethic. Under this rule, touchstone represents a human value, the ethic. In order to receive the bonus from this background, the vampire must have been acting in service to one of their ethics. This rule allows for the addition of Convictions and Tenets from V5 to be used in V20, but this rule can theoretically still be abused somehow. Ultimately, it is up to the Storyteller to determine how to implement this rule.</div> <br /> So in my mind, Touchstones are a short term solution to a long-term problem in vampire society. The beast is always out to get yah, and you're always at risk of losing touch with what made you, well you! As such Touchstones can help, but only for so long. After all, humans are, and most objects and places, have a finite lifespan, and don't last forever. Also the reason I didn't make this background available to Paths is due to their already specialized nature. That and the fact vampires on a Path don't want to remind themselves of their lost humanity, so why would they use this Background?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T13:37:10-07:00","id":1463614,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's a lot better. Far more elagant than how they genrally work. Good idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T14:16:34-07:00","id":1463619,"title":"","content":"I actually think it is a good addition to Paths too, so I would ignore your prohibition entirely, but otherwise good job.<br /> <br /> Yet I disagree with most of the reddit post and would do the opposite, V20 lore with V5 rules, adding modifications and taking only inspiration from V5 for metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T15:28:30-07:00","id":1463629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463612-v20-touchstone-background?p=1463619#post1463619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think it is a good addition to Paths too, so I would ignore your prohibition entirely, but otherwise good job.<br /> <br /> Yet I disagree with most of the reddit post and would do the opposite, V20 lore with V5 rules, adding modifications and taking only inspiration from V5 for metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. While I may disagree, your point is very valid and I can respect it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T20:49:38-07:00","id":1463645,"title":"","content":"I like the way Long Hard Road Out Of Hell does non-human touchstones: Path takers can have them, but they gain a Beast Mark appropriate to Path values when they take non-human touchstones. I love how this allows you to customize your lack of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T23:39:22-07:00","id":1463795,"title":"","content":"This is a very elegant and useful adaption of one of V5's innovations. I could see myself borrowing it for my own V20 chronicle!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}